### 🔴 Critical (must fix before merge)
None found.

### 🟠 Major (strongly recommended)
- `hooks/tests/dispatch-author.test.sh:242,245` + `scripts/lib/output-quiescence.sh:37` + `scripts/dispatch-author.sh:210` — The diff introduces a genuinely new per-runner default (cc-shim empty-grace = 30000ms via the new 3rd positional arg to `wait_output_quiescent`), but the **only pre-existing test that exercises cc-shim quiescence timing was not updated**. Its comment at line 242 still reads `"With default 10s wait for cc-shim, a 5s late flush should be caught"` — that claim is now false (default is 30000ms, not 10000ms, per `scripts/lib/output-quiescence.sh:37`: `grace_ms="${AUTOPILOT_EMPTY_GRACE_MS:-${3:-10000}}"` combined with the caller passing literal `30000`). Worse, none of the existing cc-shim assertions (`hooks/tests/dispatch-author.test.sh:233-267`) actually discriminate between a 10s and a 30s grace: the late-flush stub fires at 5s (passes under either bound) and the "truly-empty" assertion (`:258-261`) checks only `status`/`exit`, never elapsed time. Consequence: this is documented in the code itself as the **third occurrence** of the same empty-misclassification bug class (`scripts/lib/output-quiescence.sh:9` "Born-from note ... BACKLOG third occurrence"), yet the regression test that would catch a *fourth* occurrence (e.g. someone accidentally reverting the 3rd-arg wiring, or breaking the env>arg>default precedence) does not exist. Compare: the prior fix for this same file (`67ee388`, changelog line 9: "跨 3 檔 + lib + **test**") did add/extend tests; this fix (line 10: "(3 檔)") explicitly did not touch tests. Fix direction: add a stub case asserting the cc-shim path specifically honors the 30000ms default distinctly from other runners' 10000ms (e.g. a stub that flushes at ~15–20s: expect `empty_output`/fast-fail for a non-cc-shim runner at that delay, but `authored` for cc-shim), and correct the stale "10s"/"default" wording in `hooks/tests/dispatch-author.test.sh:242,245`.

### 🟡 Minor (recommended)
- `hooks/tests/dispatch-author.test.sh:258-261` — The "cc-shim truly-empty exits 1" case does not set `AUTOPILOT_EMPTY_GRACE_MS`, so after this diff it now blocks for the full new cc-shim default (30000ms) instead of the prior 10000ms — a ~20s CI wall-time increase for this one assertion, introduced silently by this diff. Its sibling in `hooks/tests/dispatch-output-quiescence.test.sh:99` uses `AUTOPILOT_EMPTY_GRACE_MS=1000` specifically to stay fast; this test should follow the same tuned-override convention. Fix direction: export `AUTOPILOT_EMPTY_GRACE_MS=1000` (or similar) for that assertion so the CI suite doesn't silently grow slower with every future runner-specific grace bump.

### 🔵 Suggestion (consider)
- `scripts/dispatch-author.sh:40-41` (and identical mirror `platforms/codex/plugin/scripts/dispatch-author.sh:40-41`) — Pre-existing, **not touched by this diff** (so not scope creep to require here), but directly adjacent to the exact mechanism this diff changes and now doubly confusing: the header comment claims `AUTOPILOT_SETTLE_MS` has a "default: 3000ms; cc-shim: 10000ms" — neither number matches the code, which uses a uniform `${AUTOPILOT_SETTLE_MS:-60000}` (60000ms) for every runner including cc-shim (lines 210, 212). The actual per-runner customization this diff adds is on the separate `grace_ms` 3rd argument, not `AUTOPILOT_SETTLE_MS`. Since this diff just made "per-runner override of a quiescence parameter" a real, working feature, a future reader will likely mis-map this stale comment onto the new behavior. Recommend fixing the comment while this exact function is fresh context (not blocking this commit).
- Release hygiene: the analogous prior fix to this file (`67ee388`) shipped as version `v2.31.17` with a full CHANGELOG entry; this fix is logged only in `docs/projects/ongoing-maintenance/2026-07.md` (consistent with that file's own stated S/Fix-size convention, so not a defect), but since it changes the same shipped script's runtime default, consider folding a one-line addendum into the CHANGELOG or the next release's headline so `v2.31.17`'s "10s grace" claim in `CHANGELOG.md:41` isn't left stale for readers of that entry.

