### Summary
Overall risk: Medium — the code change itself is small and logically correct (verified by hand-tracing the bash expansion and all six call sites), but it ships a fix to a bug that has now recurred three times with strictly weaker test coverage than its immediate predecessor fix, and a stale test comment that will actively mislead the next person to touch this file.

Top 3 priorities to fix:
1. Add a regression test that actually distinguishes cc-shim's new 30000ms default from other runners' 10000ms default (🟠 Major).
2. Fix the stale "10s wait for cc-shim" test comment at `hooks/tests/dispatch-author.test.sh:242,245` (part of the same Major finding).
3. Tune the now-slower "cc-shim truly-empty" test with an explicit `AUTOPILOT_EMPTY_GRACE_MS` override to avoid a silent CI wall-time regression (🟡 Minor).

